{
  "_note": "Written by the Settings modal (live pill -> Settings) and read by tools/signal_alert.py and tools/event_alert.py on every poll. Safe to hand-edit; the UI rewrites the whole file, so a comment added here will not survive a save -- put explanations in the per-cell `note` field, which does. `grade` is the cell's measured standing against its own friction floor (tools/friction_map.py + the three-era table in the README): validated | marginal | below, shown on every message so a sub-friction alert never reads like a validated one; cells added from the UI are ungraded, the honest state for a cell nobody has measured. `strategy` is OPTIONAL and PER CELL: omit it and the cell runs its timeframe's default (sim.strategies.strategy_for_tf), name one and that cell runs that rule instead. It exists because the rule was previously chosen per TIMEFRAME globally, so USDJPY 4h was handed the rule validated on XAUUSD 4h -- and USDJPY 4h measured clearly negative under it. Only strategies in sim.strategies.BASELINES can be served live; tl_breakout needs a trendline/regime table and is research-only for now. `destinations` is WHERE the alerts go: one entry per chat or WhatsApp number, each with a `channel` (telegram | whatsapp), a `target` -- for Telegram a numeric chat id, an @username, or a t.me link (t.me/name and t.me/c/<id>/<msg> are both resolved; a t.me/+hash INVITE link cannot be, and is refused); for WhatsApp a phone number in E.164 form or a wa.me link. The stored value is what was typed and is re-resolved on every send by tools/notify.py normalize_target(), and `kinds` -- any of signals | news | scalper -- so one group can take the macro calendar and not every 5m entry. Managed in Settings -> Destinations, read by tools/notify.py, which every alerting tool now sends through. A MISSING `destinations` key is not the same as an empty list: missing means nobody has configured this yet and TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID from configs/secrets.env is still the router, while [] means every destination was removed and nothing is announced anywhere. Tokens are NOT here and never will be -- they stay in configs/secrets.env, which the browser cannot read. `news.fetch_minutes` is how often the feed is refetched automatically (0 = manual only, minimum 5). It is honoured by whichever supervisor is up -- the timer in serve.py while the app is open, the `news` job in alerts_daemon.py otherwise -- and both ask `fetch_quantgist_news.py --scheduled`, which reads this value itself and compares it against the AGE OF THE FILE, so two runners cannot double the fetch rate.",
